From: Jeroen Hofstee <jhofstee@victronenergy.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove the emSign ECC Root CA - G3 certificate

Remove "emSign ECC Root CA - G3" from the bundled cacert.pem, in
response to the eMudhra intermediate CA compromise. This is the net
effect of two upstream commits:

  5cb238c Remove emsign (#437)
          removes all four emSign roots
  662df63 Restore unaffected emSign roots (#439) (#440)
          restores G1, C1 and C3, as only ECC G3 is affected

[dunfell backport: the upstream commits do not apply to 2019.11.28, so
this patch was made by hand: it removes the same "emSign ECC Root CA -
G3" block (identical serial and fingerprints) from the 2019.11.28
cacert.pem. The version bumps in certifi/__init__.py are not included.]

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/certifi/python-certifi/commit/5cb238caeeb6c30ec1a7309ad3e16a5aa7b10ce8 https://github.com/certifi/python-certifi/commit/662df63d7906df66f1f07c0751a3dfe9da14d914]
---
 certifi/cacert.pem | 23 -----------------------
 1 file changed, 23 deletions(-)

--- a/certifi/cacert.pem
+++ b/certifi/cacert.pem
